"Wardrobe is a Rabbit perk giving easy access to armor-like alien clothing that raises stats."
"Its items are costly."
"Otherwise only a few hardcore battle subclasses get armor, and only after leveling."
"The Wardrobe is a Rabbit-exclusive marketplace, not a personal storage space."
"Its items are work uniforms more than armor."
"Every item gives +1 or more Sympathy for Magic; many add +0.5 to another stat."
"Its passive reduces the magic needed to summon the wearer, making summons likelier."
"Wearing one chosen job outfit every day is ideal."
"Storage in System warehouses and teleporting items from them cost extra."
"Outfits include bartending, butler, housekeeper, tattooist's assistant and expeditioner."
"The spell Wardrobe Change swaps a Rabbit into Wardrobe gear."
"Wardrobe stat bonuses are enchantments, drawing nothing on the wearer's authority."
"The Wardrobe does not sell basics."
"Some tabs, such as knight uniforms, are available only on the Triplanets and a few worlds."
"The Wardrobe shop closes when nonessential Contract services halt."
"Wizards who summon humans, and most Anesidorans, recognize Wardrobe clothes as work clothes."
"Worn alone, Wardrobe gear marks a Rabbit hoping for summons, or one on a summons."
